umors  began to circulate online about the  cancellation of the Covenant sequels  shortly after the movie hit theaters a  December 2017 report from the fansite a  VP galaxy cited a user on the blu-ray  comm forums who claims to have worked on  covenant and explained after the box  office results filming was cancelled and  a warehouse storage unit full of stuff  was auctioned off a few months ago so  the original plan of pumping out another  quickly  has definitely changed with no immediate  plans for anything though the validity  of the statement hasn't been confirmed  there are indications that the users  account has some truth to it and the  film was either cancelled or put on hold  I think it's safe to say that none of us  are too keen on getting back at one of  those pods before the release of alien  coming in Ridley Scott spoke with  Fandango saying if this is successful  and then the next one there will  definitely be three more this could mean  a projected total of six prequel films  before the events of the original alien  but only if covenant was a success  Fandango wasn't the only place Scott  showed his excitement for the future of  the alien series in an interview with  The Sydney Morning Herald he enthused if  you really want a franchise I can keep  cranking it for another six I'm not  going to close it down again no way  that's what I'm going is that is not the  plan because I'm really right I've heard  the next one is what if they don't know  to drive the point home he talked about  having written the next installment  saying you've got to assume to a certain  extent success and from that you'd  better be ready  of course regardless of Scotts readiness  it was soon apparent that covenant was  not going to be as successful as its  predecessor putting the future of the  series in question further complicating  the matter that Disney Foxx merger was  finalized in early 2019 reliable  information regarding the status of a  covenant sequel has been sparse 